\name{cellucid_history_search}
\alias{cellucid_history_search}
\title{Search the history}
\usage{
cellucid_history_search(
  viewer,
  bookmarked,
  by,
  domain,
  flagged,
  has_note,
  kind,
  step_kind,
  text,
  tracker
)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{bookmarked}{\code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{by}{Who took them. One of \code{"person"}, \code{"agent"}, \code{"python"}, \code{"r"}, \code{"replay"}, \code{"outside"}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{domain}{The part of the state they changed. One of \code{"cells"}, \code{"mapping"}, \code{"field-overlays"}, \code{"gene-sets"}, \code{"views"}, \code{"active-field"}, \code{"filters"}, \code{"colors"}, \code{"visibility"}, \code{"highlights"}, \code{"camera"}, \code{"camera-path"}, \code{"settings"}, \code{"analysis"}, \code{"layout"}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{flagged}{Stale, or no longer applying. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{has_note}{\code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{kind}{What their action changes. One of \code{"state"}, \code{"view"}, \code{"layout"}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{step_kind}{What they are: root, action, outside (changed outside an action) or squashed. One of \code{"root"}, \code{"action"}, \code{"outside"}, \code{"squashed"}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{text}{Words to find (any case). Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{tracker}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them); the tracker in use when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{steps} (The matching steps, in step order), \code{total} (Steps in the tracker), \code{tracker}. Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
The steps whose label, parameters, notes or bookmark match, filtered by who took them, their kind, the part of the state they changed, notes, bookmarks and flags.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.search} (History). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_search(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
